// a *template* owes a body just as an ordinary function does, and it is the reason the check cannot
// be spelled over AST::function_emission_kind: a template has no symbol, so `emission_has_body` is
// false for it, and this one would have slipped through. nothing instantiates a body that is not
// there, so the template is where it has to be reported
function twin<T>(T $value) : T;

echo 1;
